## 🎯 Stage 1 in one line

> *"Aircraft monitor engines and avionics with precision — nobody monitors the humans inside."*
> CabinMind AI is a per-seat, privacy-first Edge AI platform that **senses** passenger wellbeing, **predicts** risk before it escalates, and **adapts** the cabin automatically.

## ❗ The problem we chose

| Problem | Why it hurts |
|---|---|
| 😰 **Flight anxiety & panic** | 25M+ people in the US alone have aviophobia; crew only act after a visible breakdown |
| 🩺 **Undetected medical risk** | In-flight medical emergencies occur roughly 1 in 15,000–50,000 passengers; DVT risk rises after 4+ hours of immobility |
| 🌀 **Turbulence shock** | Leading cause of in-flight injuries; PA warning gives ~30 seconds |
| 😴 **Post-flight fatigue** | No airline builds a recovery plan from actual in-flight data |
| 🤐 **Silent distress** | Most distressed passengers never press the call button |

## 💡 The solution — Sense · Predict · Adapt

| Layer | What happens |
|---|---|
| **SENSE** | Seat-embedded, non-wearable sensing: HRV/heart rate, GSR, seat pressure & posture, movement, temperature, ambient noise, flight data |
| **PREDICT** | On-board Edge AI fuses signals and classifies stress, fatigue, dehydration and DVT risk; works with limited connectivity |
| **ADAPT** | Light, airflow and calming audio adjust; crew gets a discreet alert with seat, risk level and suggested action |

### Four core features
1. **Stress-Aware Cabin Adaptation** – per-seat state (calm / mild anxiety / high stress / distress) drives lighting and sound
2. **Predictive Turbulence Pre-Calming** – planned T−12 / T−8 / T−4 minute sequence instead of a ~30-second announcement
3. **Silent Medical Escalation** – immobility (DVT), dehydration proxy and panic detection trigger private crew alerts
4. **Post-Flight Fatigue & Recovery Score** – personalised recovery plan after landing

## 🔍 Does it already exist? (our research)

We benchmarked public disclosures, papers and patents from Airbus, Boeing, Collins Aerospace, Honeywell, Safran and Panasonic, plus IDTechEx research. Components exist separately (automotive emotion sensing, smart cabin lighting, seat-occupancy AI, turbulence forecasting). **We did not find a public system that combines per-passenger physiological sensing, Edge AI, adaptive cabin response, crew alerting and post-flight recovery in one embedded platform.** *(This is a team review of public sources, not a legal patent search.)*

## 🧪 Stage 1 proof of concept (runs on a laptop)

A runnable **local simulation** of the Sense → Predict → Adapt pipeline, no AWS account needed.

- **`simulator.py`** generates a synthetic **4-hour flight, 24 seats** (HRV, GSR, movement)
- **`dashboard.html`**: live crew dashboard with cabin heat map, alerts, turbulence banner, play/pause/scrub and 3x/8x speed. **Double-click to open.**

Scripted events: stress spike at ~T+35 (red) · dehydration flag at ~T+92 (amber) · DVT-risk flag at ~T+150 (amber) · turbulence pre-calm sequence at ~T+228 to T+240.

⚠️ **Honest status:** simulated data only. Not a live AWS demo, and no physical hardware at Stage 1.

