## 🏗️ Planned tech stack (Stage 1 vision)

Embedded sensing (HRV, GSR, pressure, IMU, temperature, noise) → on-board Edge AI (sensor fusion; Random Forest, XGBoost, LSTM, anomaly detection) → AWS (IoT Core, Lambda, SageMaker, DynamoDB, S3, API Gateway) → React dashboards. Python, scikit-learn, TensorFlow, NumPy, Pandas.

## 🔄 How Stage 1 became Stage 2

| Stage 1 (vision) | Stage 2 (what we built) |
|---|---|
| Broad sensor suite incl. IR/thermal and microphone | Focused, low-cost **4-sensor rig** (MAX30102, GSR, FSR-402, MPU-6050) + LED/buzzer on an ESP32, Rs 1,850 |
| ML model options listed | **Random Forest trained**: 90.3% accuracy, 86.4% macro F1 *(synthetic data)* |
| Laptop-only simulated dashboard | **Deployed web app**, 3D cabin twin, passenger companion, Copilot |
| AWS pipeline planned | AWS ingest/read Lambda **code written and unit-tested** |
| Privacy as a principle | Privacy enforced in firmware and cloud code (raw data stays on the seat, opt-in consent) |

## 🔒 Privacy principle (since day one)

Passengers opt in; raw biometrics never leave the seat unit — only classified states are transmitted.

